--[[
        C R U C I F I X   S P A W N E R        -- the realistic one

        Hides a crucifix in the furniture. Rummage through drawers and
        wardrobes like you already do, and occasionally one is in there.

        Loaded once per run by Main script. For a crucifix on demand while you
        are building an entity, use CrucifixGiver instead -- that one just
        hands it to you.

        HOW IT FINDS FURNITURE
        ----------------------
        It hooks ProximityPromptService.PromptTriggered, and the matching is no
        longer guesswork -- it was read out of a place dump of the game:

            Dresser / Drawer / Table      <Model>
              DrawerContainer             <Model>
                Knobs                     <MeshPart>
                  ActivateEventPrompt     <ProximityPrompt>   ActionText "Open"
                LootHolder > SpawnPile                        ObjectText "Drawer"

        The prompt sits inside Knobs, which is why it does not show up in a
        screenshot of DrawerContainer's children and why this went unconfirmed
        for so long. Drawer x20, Dresser x12, Table x2 in that dump.

        Hints below are now only a last-resort fallback.
]]

local Core = loadstring(game:HttpGet(
	"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/main/GradishCore"
))()

Core.Crucifix:EnableDrawers({
	--[[ The odds climb as you search.

	     A flat percentage was wrong both ways: you open dozens of drawers in a
	     run, so a flat 12% found you one almost immediately, and an unlucky
	     run could still turn up nothing after fifty. Starting at 4% and adding
	     1.2% per drawer means early searching is rarely rewarded, persistent
	     searching always pays off eventually, and neither result feels random.

	     Roughly: half of runs have found one by the tenth drawer searched. ]]
	Chance        = 0.04, -- where it starts
	RampPerSearch = 0.012, -- added for each drawer that came up empty
	MaxChance     = 0.40, -- and it stops climbing here

	-- Nothing before this room. A crucifix in the first few rooms trivialises
	-- everything that comes after it.
	MinRoom = 10,

	-- How many can be found in a single run. One keeps it precious, which is
	-- the whole point of it being a find rather than a button.
	MaxPerRun = 1,

	-- It goes in your backpack, not your hand. Finding it and choosing to
	-- hold it are two different decisions.
	AutoEquip = false,

	-- Wait for the drawer to finish opening before it appears.
	Delay = 0.35,

	-- Prints every prompt you trigger, the odds of each roll, and whether the
	-- drawer still had its clutter in it.
	Debug = false,

	-- Fallback only. The exact checks above catch every drawer in the dump;
	-- these exist in case a room variant is built some other way.
	Hints = {
		"drawer", "dresser", "wardrobe", "cabinet", "closet",
		"chest", "desk", "shelf", "bin", "nightstand", "locker", "table",
	},

	-- Set true to let ANY prompt roll, ignoring the names entirely. Blunt,
	-- but it works everywhere while you are figuring out the right words.
	AnyPrompt = false,
})
